oduction company.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20020958422 aAC Films (New York, N.Y.),eproduction company.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20180998692 aLB Entertainment (Firm),eproduction company.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20230841952 aWild7 Films,eproduction company.2 aRelativity Media,epublisher.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no2007002471  aZ0bSTF  hNO HOLDINGS IN STF - 109 OTHER HOLDINGSffi25a0eacb-bf44-422a-b698-776656763544s84e48ab3-71cc-441d-93af-6471a741851d06729nab a2200853ui in0000030270420250403135007.0m||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu231023s2023||||xx || | |||||||   ||eng|d  als144916  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00ae-flux Journal #139 1a[Place of publication not identified] :be-flux,c2023  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 ae-flux journal ;v139  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"If you believe in progress, the old and aged are always to blame for causing the persistent problems of the present, and the young, who supposedly come later, are the solution. This is all very tidy until you wake up one day to find yourself old-and observe that the young who blame you are also the young who are causing the problems of the future, just as you had in your own youth. In this issue, Luis Camnitzer offers advice to the aging-which, to be clear, means all of us-through an anecdotal contribution to the field of intergenerational dialogic studies. He discusses attempts at nonauthoritarian child rearing; his experience, while a student activist, of explaining an art historian's own obsolescence to his face; and recent moments when he's realized that his generation has become ineffective at communicating with the young. In other words, Camnitzer fears that his has become the generation suffering from "asshole syndrome"-a diagnosis he and his fellow students used to dole out. Age and power together form a complex configuration, which make empathy and self-assessment all the more important when communicating across generational lines... Editorial Editors Geriatric Power Luis Camnitzer No Order Makes Any Sense: A Conversation on Ilya Kabakov Boris Groys and Anton Khitrov Politics at Sunset: Theses on Benjamin Mario Tronti Hospicing Modernity: A Conversation Vanessa Machado de Oliveira Andreotti and Lucia Pietroiusti Anarcho-Ecstasy: Options for an Afri-Queer Becoming KJ Abudu Racial Fascism Alberto Toscano Capitalism and Schismogenesis, Part 2 Sven Lütticken Never Born Shane Greene"--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aArt criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500798910aArtxHistory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500748810aEcology.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8504075210aHistorical materialism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506119610aHistoriography.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506121110aImperialism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506462810aRacism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8511026610aSexual minority culture.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh201910354217aArt criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008154920http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81549217aArt History.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0081539617aColonies.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009681260http://id.worldcat.org/fast/86845617aEcology.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009014760http://id.worldcat.org/fast/90147617aHistorical materialism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009581410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/95814117aHistoriography.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009582210http://id.worldcat.org/fast/95822117aSexual minority culture.2fast0(OCoLC)fst020108600http://id.worldcat.org/fast/201086017aRacism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010866160http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1086616 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/