ory of Synthetic Cognition 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bOnassis Foundation,c2022  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"A volume on artificial intelligence, which attempts to disassemble and reformulate what one might understand as AI by taking apart both notions of 'artificiality' and 'intelligence' and seeing what new meaning they produce when recombined. We summon the trickster of the natural order, chimera, both a mythical creature and a genetic phenomenon. Drawing upon chimerism allows us to broaden 'artificial intelligence' into 'synthetic cognition'⁠-an approach that highlights the duality of 'artificial' and 'authentic', amplifies non-human methods of cognition and anticipates modes of symbiosis. With this aim, the editors, Ilan Manouach and Anna Engelhardt, assembled an inventory in which one can find contributions from scholars and artists with interspecies, disability, monstrous, feminist, and decolonial approaches, as well as thinkers and technologists engaged in a broader field of AI. By questioning fabricated norms that constitute and maintain notions of 'artificial' and 'intelligence', this inventory acts as a toolbox one can use to merge these terms into a novel chimera."--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aArtificial intelligence.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500818010aArtists' writings.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500830610aCloud computing.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh200800488310aComputational intelligence.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9400465910aComputer networks.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8502951310aData mining.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9700207310aNatural language processing (Computer science)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800242510aTransborder data flow.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8600763517aArtificial intelligence.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008172470http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81724717aArtists' Writing.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0081770717aCloud computing.2fast0(OCoLC)fst017458990http://id.worldcat.org/fast/174589917aComputation.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0087199517aData mining.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008879460http://id.worldcat.org/fast/88794617aNatural Language Processing.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0103436517aNetworks.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0087229717aTransborder Data Flows.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01154519 7aDiscursive works.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026089 7aBook.2marcgt 7aCritical Writing.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01411635 7aEssay Collection.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014240321 aAllado-McDowell, K,econtributor.1 aAllen, Jamie,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n979035591 aAl-Sabah, Bassam,econtributor.1 aAnikina, Alexandra,econtributor.1 aApprich, Clemens,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20120538891 aArellano, Sadie-Mae,econtributor.1 aArgüelles, Cris,econtributor.1 aAzelmat, Marwa,econtributor.1 aBanner, Olivia,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20171860001 aBazargali, Medina,econtributor.1 aBehar, Katherine,econtributor.1 aBoichak, Olga,econtributor.1 aBounegru, Liliana,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20120841831 aBousquet, Antoine,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no980803191 aBrain, Tega,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20200332751 aBühlmann, Vera,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20040092831 aBunz, Mercedes,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20100028271 aCarver, Louise Emily,econtributor.1 aCavia, AA,econtributor.1 aCheng, Guo,econtributor.1 aColquhoun, Matt,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20200843931 aCovelli, Juan,econtributor.1 aCramer, Florian,econtributor.