ontributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20230454451 aVanable, Ife,eeditor.2 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/avery-review-issue-56-the/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls12605742uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Avery-Review-480x160.pngzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi2dca680b-f906-4dd3-9606-c08d192a2fcbs9d3b0c97-9d53-42b9-978e-493d10a40c4506279nab a2200829ui in0000029970820250403135030.0m||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu241104s2024||||xx || | |||||||   ||eng|d  als182027  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00ae-flux Journal #147 1a[Place of publication not identified] :be-flux,c2024  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 ae-flux journal ;v147  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"In this issue of e-flux journal, Trevor Paglen begins his three-part essay on how US military psychological warfare techniques were a historical predecessor to today's AI-driven social media trained to identify emotions and exploit affects. Telling the story of Richard Doty, a counterintelligence officer who deliberately spread disinformation about extraterrestrials as cover for military operations, Paglen identifies a key tenet of the US Army Field Manual: it is easier to deceive someone by reinforcing their preexisting beliefs than to change those beliefs. Behind the outlandish but well-documented example of UFO sightings lies a chilling warning that the creation of an entirely new reality is accomplished not through coercion but through the tactical use of affirmative encouragement. Editorial Editors Society of the Psyop, Part 1: UFOs and the Future of Media Trevor Paglen Planetarization and Heimatlosigkeit, Part 1 Yuk Hui Agrarian Economies and Indigenous Textiles: The Feminization of Land Struggles María Iñigo Clavo Empire's Island, or, Who Is the Island? Jonas Staal On Paralysis, Part 3 Evan Calder Williams Unworldliness: A Pathology of Humankind (On Günther Anders's Negative Anthropology) Hunter Bolin Stemming the Tide of STEM Luis Camnitzer"--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aArtificial intelligence.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500818010aCritical theory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800245610aEcology.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8504075210aElectronic surveillance in art.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh200300004610aElectronic surveillance.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8600664110aImperialism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506462810aMilitary-industrial complex.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800156910aPhilosophy.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8510084910aWar.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8514511417aArtificial intelligence.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008172470http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81724717aColonies.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009681260http://id.worldcat.org/fast/86845617aCritical theory.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008836900http://id.worldcat.org/fast/88369017aEcology.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009014760http://id.worldcat.org/fast/90147617aElectronic surveillance.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009074770http://id.worldcat.org/fast/90747717aMilitary-industrial complex.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010216050http://id.worldcat.org/fast/102160517aPhilosophy.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010607770http://id.worldcat.org/fast/106077717aSurveillance in art.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009074830http://id.worldcat.org/fast/200999317aWar.2fast0(OCoLC)fst011703280http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1170328 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/141164117aImperialism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009681260http://id.worldcat.org/fast/96812617aWorld politics.2fast0(OCoLC)fst011813810http://id.worldcat.org/fast/11813811 aAndrews, Michael,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n850118601 aAranda, Julieta,eeditor,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20061296571 aBolin, Hunter,econtributor.1 aCamnitzer, Luis,econtributor.1 aClavo, María Iñigo,econtributor.1 aFlorin, Adam,econtributor.1 aHui, Yuk,econtributor.1 aMoses, Serubiri,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20191245191 aNguyễn, Minh,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n980829811 aPaglen, Trevor,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20061125021 aPetrossiants, Andreas,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20181752121 aQian, Mengyi,econtributor.1 aRamsey, Jeff,econtributor.1 aSit, Peter,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20240306961 aStaal, Jonas,econtributor.1 aVafai, Keyian,econtributor.1 aVidokle, Anton,eeditor,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20061296551 aWhite, Simone,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb970923831 aWilk, Elvia,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20170235181 aWilliams, Evan Calder,econtributor,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20111190571 aWood, Brian Kuan,eeditor,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20110095182 aLibrary Stack,edistributor. 0aE-flux journal (Series) ;v147.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no201116589040zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/e-flux-journal-147/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls18202742uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/e-flux-147-cvr-480x621.pngzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi2f4cd09b-7a37-4711-8677-e00671459477s78e37696-cffb-4bd5-97da-d56367b62ab406945nab a2200841ui in0000030162520250403135034.0m||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu231023s2019||||xx || | |||||||   ||eng|d  als144849  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00ae-flux Journal #105 1a[Place of publication not identified] :be-flux,c2019  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 ae-flux journal ;v105  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"On April 27, 2019, the Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum was the site of a very special convening. It was the brainchild of Simone Leigh, and shared its title with her 2019 exhibition at the museum. Organized by Leigh, Saidiya Hartman, and myself, "The Loophole of Retreat" was an exhilarating, rejuvenating, and inspirational daylong gathering dedicated to the intellectual life of black women that brought together an international constellation of writers, artists, poets, filmmakers, and activists. This special issue of e-flux journal seeks to lift up the extraordinary voices, thoughts, and conversations that emerged at the convening and share them with a wider audience. In doing so, I and my coeditors, Leigh and Hartman, seek to extend the dialogues of the "Loophole" in the hope of including others and inspiring future gatherings which, like the Guggenheim convening, will honor and celebrate the intellectual and creative labor of black women... The Loophole of Retreat-An Invitation Tina M. Campt Extended Notes on the Riot Saidiya Hartman Images from "Loophole of Retreat" Simone Leigh bound together by this matter Simone White The Music of the Spheres Sharifa Rhodes-Pitts A Gathering of Aporetic Form Rizvana Bradley Maps Dionne Brand Suspended Munition: Mereology, Morphology, and the Mammary Biopolitics of Transmission in Simone Leigh's Trophallaxis Zakiyyah Iman Jackson Beauty Is a Method Christina Sharpe Selvage/Obsidian: A Response Vanessa Agard-Jones Still images from ILLUSIONS Vol. II, OEDIPUS Grada Kilomba Politics of Marooning and Radical Disobedience Françoise Vergès How Denise Ferreira da Silva of wishing and superheroes Okwui Okpokwasili Interstice Lorraine O'Grady Reflections on Black Sisterhood and the United Order of Tents Annette Lane Harrison Richter Still images from Spit on the Broom Madeleine Hunt-Ehrlich the order was in the hour of worship Asiya Wadud"--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aArt criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500798910aFeminism and art.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8504774610aFeminist theory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9000228210aRacism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8511026610aVideo art.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8514319510aViolence.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8514351417aArt criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008154920http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81549217aFeminism and art.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009227270http://id.worldcat.org/fast/92272717aFeminist theory.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009228160http://id.worldcat.org/fast/92281617aRacism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010866160http://id.worldcat.org/fast/108661617aVideo art.2fast0(OCoLC)fst011663890http://id.worldcat.org/fast/116638917aViolence.2fast0(OCoLC)fst011672240http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1167224 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/14116411 aAgard-Jones, Vanessa,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20080191981 aAndrews, Michael,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n850118601 aAranda, Julieta,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20061296571 aBradley, Rizvana,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20180324691 aBrand, Dionne,econtributor.1 aCain-Nielsen, Kaye,eeditor.1 aCampt, Tina M.,eeditor,econtributor.1 a