esiderat.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200106026412iContainer of (work):aKnüpfer, Sebastian,d1633-1676.tSuper flumina Babylonis.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200106026712iContainer of (work):aKnüpfer, Sebastian,d1633-1676.tJesus Christus, unser Heiland.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200106026812iContainer of (work):aKnüpfer, Sebastian,d1633-1676.tTurteltaube lässt sich hören.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20010602692 aKing's Consort,eperformer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr8901725708iSource record:aKnüpfer, Sebastian, 1633-1676.sVocal music. Selections.tSacred music.dLondon : Hyperion, [2011]w(OCoLC)77506769840zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttp://stanford.naxosmusiclibrary.com/catalogue/item.asp?cid=00602458145960yNaxos Music LibraryxProvider: NaxosxCollection: Naxos Music LibraryxsubscribedxeLoaderURLxnm4xnmon1459744244  aeLoaderRecord xnm4ffi34a4e50f-a222-4c90-9628-15068b627a8fs0a4e31c7-1c74-482d-9dbf-fad334d8d71c07993nab a2201189ui in0000030123120250403135044.0m||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu170102s2004||||xx || | |||||||   ||eng|d  als7082  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aSarai Reader 04: Crisis/Media 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bSarai, CSDS,c2004  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aSarai Reader ;v4  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a""The book itself has its genesis in the Crisis/Media Workshop that was jointly organized in Delhi by Sarai-CSDS, Delhi and the Waag Society, Amsterdam, a year ago in March 2003. The concept, outlined in the workshop publication by Shuddhabrata Sengupta and Geert Lovink, was a response to 9/11, the invasion of Afghanistan, the violence in Gujarat and the Kargil war. Over 3 days, participants from many different parts of South Asia and the world gathered to debate and dissect the relationship between the notion of crisis and the media, exactly one year after Gujarat had gone up in flames, and just as the 'Coalition of the Willing' was gearing up to bomb Baghdad. The process of editing the Reader only confirmed what we felt that the workshop had already set in motion - an unruly but very necessary set of forays into the realm of 'the unspeakable'. Our contributors were opening out new spaces for dialogue, not only by inaugurating discussion on things that had hitherto been left unsaid, but also in the way that different elements were speaking to each other. Our task was to enable this conversation to interrupt itself, to make all sorts of unruly connections, to foster linkages between disparate truths and conflicting claims to attention...""--cprovided by distributor  aCC BY-NC-SA10aCritical theory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800245617aCritical theory.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008836900http://id.worldcat.org/fast/883690 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/14116411 aAdajania, Nancy,eauthor.1 aAgarwal, Ravi,eauthor.1 aAhmed, Shakeb,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20142104801 aAmin, Shahid,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n841919731 aAnsari, Rehan,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20210078071 aBagchi, Jeebesh,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20062056081 aBarentsen, Sasja,eauthor.1 aBawa, Zainab,eauthor.1 aBhartiya, Tarun,eauthor.1 aBrosius, Christiane,eauthor.1 aChan, Paul,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780303151 aChatterji, Subarno,eauthor.1 aCorrie, Rachel,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20040298531 aCox, Geoff,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20030104251 aDa Costa, Beatriz,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20070554561 aDesai, Darshan,eauthor.0