er.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790247372 aRadioorkestern (Sweden),eperformer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n841309502 aRadiotjänst (Sweden).bSymfoniorkester,eperformer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n84162354  aRobert Baxter collection  aSUL/MUSIC/catalogedby/Flourish-CAM/202410  aSUL/MUSIC/gift/kevkishi/20241106/Baxter  b36105234615941cMCD 74460n1lMusic PAGE-MU (MUS-PAGE-MU)  aC0bSTFffsd60b7f41-129a-467c-9074-fd987bf52e3bi427aca46-27cf-42f4-9001-53a16a271ccf06957nab a2201069ui in0000030029620250403135120.0m||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu161228s2002||||xx || | |||||||   ||eng|d  als6983  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aSarai Reader 02: The Cities of Everyday Life 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bSarai, CSDS,c2002  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aSarai Reader ;v2  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"This year's Sarai Reader brings together a range of critical thinking on urban life and the contemporary, marked by spreading media cultures, new social conflict and globalisation. Scholars, media practitioners, critics and activists use a flow of images, memories and hidden realities to create a fascinating array of original interventions in thinking about cities today. In the context of India, where a large part of this reader has been edited, this is significant, given the frugality of writing on city life in this part of the world. With essays, images, analyses, and manifestoes The Cities of Everyday Life reflects on the contemporary urban condition, detours into the back alleys of the global city, takes on media representations of terror and war, examines the politics of information, anticipates the futures of digital urbanism, registers the details of media flows, explores representations of the city, and looks at globalisation from below."--cprovided by distributor  aCC BY-NC-SA10aCity planning.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8502628210aCritical theory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800245610aPolitical science.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8510444017aCritical theory.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008836900http://id.worldcat.org/fast/88369017aPolitical science.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010697810http://id.worldcat.org/fast/106978117aUrbanism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00862177 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/14116411 aAkanni, Niji,eauthor.1 aʻAlī, Shamsher,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20072123761 aArif, Yasmeen,eauthor.1 aArnison, Mathew,eauthor.1 aBagchi, Jeebesh,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20062056081 aBazaz, Abir,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20050450121 aBerardi, Franco "Bifo",eauthor.1 aBhargava, Rajeev,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n910869881 aBouman, Ole,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr940203821 aCaroll, Brian,eauthor.1 aChatterjee, Joy,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr980311051 aDas, Veena,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780549261 aDasgupta, Rana,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n801580761 ade Silva, Sam,eauthor.1 aDeer, Patrick,eauthor.1 aFuller, Matthew,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n931222421 aGanguly, Avishek,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20220634231 aGill, Gagan,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n892027921 aGovil, Nitin,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20140683561 aHahn, Dorothea,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20170310891 aHansen, Kathryn,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n910326411 aHaskel, Lisa,eauthor.1 aHenshaw-Plath, Evan,eauthor.1 aIlich, Fran,eauthor.1 aJoshi, Sopan,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20062070461 aLovink, Geert,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr980175101 aLyon, David,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n822692271 aMazumdar, Ranjani,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n979218201 aMazzarella, William,eauthor.1 aMiller, Toby,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20120171711 aNandy, Ashis,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790782911 aNarula, Monica,eeditor,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20062061231 aNigam, Aditya,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20060203171 aPrakash, Gyan,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n500219911 aPrakash, Uday,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no000491831 aRai, Suraj,eauthor.1 aRajan, Kaushik Sunder,eauthor.1 aSchneider, Florian,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20150260571 aSengupta, Debjani,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20010882871 aSengupta, Shuddhabrata,eeditor,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20111033961 aSharan, Awadhendra,eauthor.1 aSharma, Parvati,eauthor.1 aSik, Cho Im,eauthor.1 aSingh, Bhrigupati,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20131195361 aSpuybroek, Lars,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20010105261 aSrinivas, K. Ravi,eauthor.1 aSubramaniam, Radhika,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20090989601 aSundaram, Ravi,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n841099031 aTabassum, Azra,eauthor.1 aVasudevan, Ravi S,eeditor.1 aVasudevan, Ravi S.,eauthor.1 aVirilio, Paul,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n810105771 aWark, McKenzie,eauthor.2 aArchimedia,eAuthor.2 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.2 aRAQS Media Collective,eAuthor. 0aSarai reader ;v2.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200108782640zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/sarai-reader-02-the-cities-of-everyday-life/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls698342uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/12/sarai_reader_02-240x350.jpgzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi4335a5b3-7c34-4d6c-94cd-ec9ea6cf4bbfsd028185e-795c-44bd-aca6-836dc27bad1f06604cam a2200637 i in0000008640220250403135122.0240521t20242024mx a          000 0 eng d  a9788419233103qpaperback  a8419233102qpaperback 9agls20807889  a(OCoLC-M)1437292661  aTOHbengerdacTOHdC3LdILOdOCLCOdYDXdCStdUtOrBLW  an-us--- 4aTR820.5b.O546 202414a77921400aOmen :bphantasmagoria at the Farm Security Administration Archive 1935-1942 : excavations at the Miriam and Ira D. Wallach Division of Art, Prints and Photographs of the New York Public Library /cphotographs by Russell Lee, Dorothea Lange, Ben Shahn, Walker Evans, Carl Mydans, Arthur Rothstein, Gordon Parks ; text by Lucy Ives ; edited by Léon Muñoz Santini [and] Pablo Ortíz Monasterio ; concept and selection by Léon Muñoz Santini [and] Jorge Panchoaga30aPhantasmagoria at the Farm Security Administration Archive 1935-1944 :bexcavations at the Miriam and Ira D. Wallach Division of Art, Prints and Photographs of the New York Public Library  aFirst edition 1aMexico City :bGato Negro Ediciones ;aBarcelona :bEditiorial RM,c[2024] 4c©2024  a158 pages :bblack and white illustrations ;c34 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aDrawing from approximately 40,000 works of the Farm Security Administration Photographic Archive (1935-42) housed at the New York Public Library, Omen reviews and reframes this landmark project of modern American documentary photography. The monumental project features works by storied photographers such as Russell Lee, Dorothea Lange, Ben Shahn, Walker Evans, Carl Mydans, Arthur Rothstein, Gordon Parks and Jack Delano. Many of the more iconic images that arose from this initiative were instrumental in constructing a hegemonic narrative of triumph against adversity in Depression-era America. In scrutinizing the backgrounds and secondary characters of some lesser-known photographs, however, a more turbulent story emerges. Omen is co-edited by Mexican artists Le̤n Mųoz Santini and Jorge Panchoaga, providing a fresh perspective on this quintessentially American study. The image sequence amplifies the eerie details in enlarged, stark black-and-white images, creatively cropped and abutted together to form insidious connections. These hidden stories are premonitions of the visible and invisible specters of systemic injustice that characterize American society, their cycles renewing with each successive generation. Thus, Omen at once serves as a mirror for the anguished reality of today, and as a device for reflection on how historical and documentary photography is read and understood: taking the editorial gaze to its ultimate consequences. The book includes a narrative text by novelist and poet Lucy Ives. -Publisher10aLee, Russell,d1903-1986.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8530673410aLange, Dorothea.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7910015910aShahn, Ben,d1898-1969.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7908508410aEvans, Walker,d1903-1975.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n5000915510aMydans, Carl.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7907283910aRothstein, Arthur,d1915-1985.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7909384410aParks, Gordon,d1912-2006.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7909009520aNew York Public Library.bMiriam and Ira D. Wallach Division of Art, Prints, and Photographs.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8785143010aUnited States.bFarm Security AdministrationxHistory. 0aBlack-and-white photographyzUnited Statesy20th century. 0aDocumentary photographyzUnited StatesxHistoryy20th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009123626 0aUnited StatesxRural conditions.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140507 6aPhotographie en noir et blanc0(CaQQLa)201-0326480zÉtats-Unis0(CaQQLa)201-0407727y20e siècle.0(CaQQLa)201-0373677 6aPhotographie documentaire0(CaQQLa)201-0048943zÉtats-Unis0(CaQQLa)201-0407727xHistoire0(CaQQLa)201-0378892y20e siècle.0(CaQQLa)201-03788921 aLee, Russell,d1903-1986,ephotogrpaher.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n853067341https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJv8HrVMkFMFQJTHbQv8md1 aLange, Dorothea,ephotographer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n791001591https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJr3pjVJDJTdPCtXcmyTpP1 aShahn, Ben,d1898-1969,ephotographer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790850841https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJgxrRC4qCcqVVDJBq8jYP1 aEvans, Walker,d1903-1975,ephotographer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n500091551https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJqk4YyrmHDKDwcdxtMQMP1 aMydans, Carl,ephotographer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790728391https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJyt4HMDjDfXrypV9gpXVC1 aRothstein, Arthur,d1915-1985,ephotographer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790938441https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJfgYXydBwRCcxWmRb7rbd1 aParks, Gordon,d1912-2006,ephotographer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790900951https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJdx4qY6fQPd8xf7WgVt8C1 aIves, Lucy,d1980-eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20090001571https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJhhqtjJFfcvK3gX3jKGHC1 aMuñoz Santini, León,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20140904611https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjBdcFpJ6pRkpDJhT4CJDq1 aOrtiz Monasterio, Pablo,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n861212621https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJp9tMx88jYKJjPXFyYgKd2 aNew Yor